---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---

<Page
	title="Privacy Policy | Gbam"
	description="How Gbam handles your data. Your files are processed in your browser and are never uploaded to us."
	heading="Privacy Policy"
	updated={site.updated}
>
	<p>This page explains what happens to your information when you use Gbam. We have tried to keep it clear and short.</p>

	<h2>The short version</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>The tools run in your browser. <strong>Your files are not uploaded to Gbam.</strong></li>
		<li>We do not ask you to create an account, and we do not ask for your name or phone number to use the tools.</li>
		<li>What you type into a tool, such as an invoice or CV, is not sent to us or stored by us.</li>
		<li>Gbam does not set its own cookies. If ads are shown, advertising partners may use cookies (see "Advertising").</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>Your files and what you type</h2>
	<p>
		When you choose a file or type into a form on a Gbam tool (a PDF, a photo, an invoice or CV), the work is done by
		your own browser on your own device. The file and the text stay in your device's memory, and they disappear when you
		close or refresh the page. We do not receive them, we cannot see them, and we do not keep copies.
	</p>
	<p>
		The AI background tool on the passport photo page needs a model file to work. Your browser downloads that file from
		our own website once and keeps it. Your photo is not sent anywhere while the model runs.
	</p>

	<h2>Information we and our hosting provider receive</h2>
	<p>
		Like every website, when you visit Gbam your browser makes a request to our hosting provider, Cloudflare. This
		normally includes your IP address, the page you asked for, the date and time, and technical details such as your
		browser type. This is needed to deliver the page and keep the site secure.
	</p>
	<p>
		We also use or plan to use privacy-friendly analytics from Cloudflare (Cloudflare Web Analytics) to count visits and
		see which pages are popular. According to Cloudflare, it does not use cookies and does not track you across other
		websites. You can read more at <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/web-analytics/">cloudflare.com/web-analytics</a>.
	</p>

	<h2>Cookies and similar technologies</h2>
	<p>
		Gbam itself does not set cookies and does not store data in your browser's local storage to track you. Your browser
		may keep downloaded site files (including the AI model file) in its cache so pages load faster. You can clear that
		in your browser settings at any time.
	</p>

	<h2>Advertising</h2>
	<p>
		Gbam may show ads provided by Google AdSense or other advertising partners to help pay for the site. If ads are
		shown, these partners may use cookies or similar technology to show ads based on your visits to this and other
		websites. Google's use of advertising cookies lets it and its partners show ads based on your visit to Gbam and
		other sites on the internet.
	</p>
	<ul>
		<li>You can manage or turn off personalised ads in <a href="https://adssettings.google.com/">Google Ads Settings</a>.</li>
		<li>
			You can also opt out of many third-party ad vendors at <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/">aboutads.info/choices</a>.
		</li>
		<li>
			To learn how Google uses data from sites that use its services, see
			<a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites">policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites</a>.
		</li>
	</ul>
	<p>Where the law requires it, we will ask for your consent before showing personalised ads.</p>

	<h2>If you contact us</h2>
	<p>
		If you email us, we receive your email address and the message you send. We use them only to reply to you and to
		improve Gbam. We keep messages only as long as we need them. Please do not email us private documents or photos.
	</p>

	<h2>Links to other websites</h2>
	<p>
		Gbam may link to other websites. We are not responsible for their content or privacy practices, so please read their
		policies.
	</p>

	<h2>Children</h2>
	<p>Gbam is not aimed at children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect personal information from them.</p>

	<h2>Your rights</h2>
	<p>
		Depending on where you live, such as under the Nigeria Data Protection Act 2023 or the EU and UK GDPR, you may have
		the right to ask what personal data we hold about you, to correct it, or to ask us to delete it. Because Gbam does
		not collect your files or an account profile, there is usually little to share, but if you want to ask, email us at
		<a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
	</p>

	<h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
	<p>
		We may update this page as Gbam changes, for example when we add new tools or start showing ads. The date at the top
		shows when it was last changed.
	</p>

	<h2>Contact</h2>
	<p>Questions about privacy? Email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> or visit our <a href="/contact">Contact page</a>.</p>
</Page>
